  <data name="Gains_Disclaimer" xml:space="preserve"><value>Figures prepared from your orders, &lt;strong&gt;not tax advice&lt;/strong&gt;. Each sale is matched to the oldest shares bought first (FIFO, Código do IRS art. 43.º). Purchases and sales are in euros at the ECB rate of their own dates; broker and currency conversion fees are expenses. Only sales are taxed: open positions are not declared. Check against the form instructions for the year.</value></data>
  <data name="Gains_EtfCodeNote" xml:space="preserve"><value>ETFs use code G20 (fund units), whose wording fits best; G90 and G01 are also used, and all three are taxed alike. To confirm.</value></data>
  <data name="Gains_Exclusion" xml:space="preserve"><value>Partial exclusion</value></data>
  <data name="Gains_ExclusionNote" xml:space="preserve"><value>Partial exclusion (Código do IRS art. 43.º n.º 5, since 29 June 2024): 10 % of the gain on listed securities held 2 to 5 years, 20 % for 5 to 8, 30 % from 8. The form asks whether the securities are listed (Sim) and the AT should apply it; the column is informative.</value></data>
